# BoardView

Accessibility product for students who can't see the classroom board. Ceiling
cameras stream to a small screen on the student's desk; teachers control it
from this web app. Read `HANDOFF.md` in the repo root for the full picture —
product intent, data model, roadmap, and what is / isn't tested.

## Stack

Next.js 16.3 (App Router, Turbopack), React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind
CSS v4, Supabase (auth + Postgres + Realtime), Stripe (hardware only),
deployed on Netlify.

**This Next.js version differs from older training data.** Version-matched
docs are bundled at `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`. Read the relevant guide
before writing routing or API code instead of relying on memory. The
`AGENTS.md` block saying this is auto-generated by `next dev` — don't remove it.

## Design rules — do not improvise

- The product must look like a restrained Apple/Google app: light, clean,
  glass-morphic. **Never** the "AI app" look — no dark mode with glowing
  accents, no neon. Light theme only, deliberately.
- **Base font-size lives on `html` (17px), never on `body`.** Tailwind's
  spacing and type scales are both rem-based off `html`; setting a size on
  `body` puts them on different scales and makes padding subtly wrong
  everywhere. This was a real bug — don't reintroduce it.
- Use the primitives in `src/components/layout.tsx` for all page structure:
  `<Section>`, `<Container size="wide|narrow|form">`, `<SectionHeader>`,
  `<Card>`. Do not hand-write `max-w-6xl px-6 py-20` on a new page.
- Design tokens and glass utilities live in `src/app/globals.css` under
  `@theme inline`. Tailwind v4 is CSS-first — there is no `tailwind.config.js`.
- Accessibility is a product requirement, not polish: keep the skip link,
  `:focus-visible` rings, real `<label>`s, `aria-label` on icon-only buttons,
  and the `prefers-reduced-motion` block.

## Architecture

- `src/app/(site)/` — route group for everything with navbar + footer. New
  marketing/account pages go here.
- `src/app/screen/[classroomId]/` — the student's device view, fullscreen with
  no chrome. That's the only reason the route group exists.
- **`src/components/ScreenCanvas.tsx` is the single source of truth for what
  the screen displays** (`boot` / `live` / `blackout`). It's shared by the real
  screen route, the teacher's live preview, and the landing-page mocks. Change
  it there so all three stay in sync.
- Blackout state lives on `classrooms.blacked_out` and reaches the screen over
  Supabase Realtime.
- `cameras.position` is kept dense (0,1,2,…) — reorder and delete rewrite every
  affected row.

## Traps

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are inlined at **build time**. Changing them in
  Netlify does nothing without a rebuild ("Clear cache and deploy site").
  Never mark them as secret in Netlify — secret scanning will fail the build.
- Never use Supabase's `service_role` key in this project; it bypasses RLS.
- ESLint bans `setState` called synchronously inside a `useEffect` body. Set
  initial state via `useState`, or update inside a promise/event callback.
  `useClock` uses `useSyncExternalStore` for this reason.
- Use `window.location.assign(url)`, not `window.location.href = url`.
- If `next build` fails with `Cannot find module '.../page.js'` from
  `.next/dev/types/validator.ts` after moving files, `rm -rf .next`.

## Before you claim something works

Run `npx eslint .` and `npm run build`. `/screen/demo` renders the screen UI
with sample data and needs no Supabase setup.
